WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
You've drawn a production
possibilities curve before.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.430
It shows the most an economy can make when

3
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.100
all its resources are fully used.

4
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.530
Now picture the whole US economy
pressed right up against that edge.

5
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.750
What decides where that edge sits?

6
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:16.810
And if Americans spend more,

7
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.790
can real GDP keep climbing beyond it?

8
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:22.500
In this mission, you'll see
why the long-run aggregate

9
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.560
supply curve is drawn as a vertical line.

10
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.220
Then you'll use a graph
lab to move that line

11
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.250
and the PPC together.

12
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.790
Your mission: find out
what limits real GDP,

13
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.970
and whether more spending
can break through.
